@title Ninja Five-0 (USA)
@file Ninja Five-0 (U).gba
@game ANXE
@chip EEPROM
@save skip: the game only writes a 12-byte signature at boot (LOAD GAME stays greyed out on the next boot); the first real save is after clearing Mission 1-1 (bank robbery), and its exit was not found in budget (the ground-floor door leads to a closed two-storey room; the balcony door, reached by grappling under the balcony and grabbing its edge, leads to a room split by a pillar with a gunman and a solid red bag on each side)
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba

# New Game > Normal > Mission 1 (bank): briefing, then the street: slash
# the gunmen, hop the crates, jump the locker, shuriken the gunman, enter
# the ground-floor door, kill the knife man, grapple up to the upper floor
# and cut down the green gunman (2000 pts).
# Frozen on dingbat-bios + mgba only: nba runs the briefing text a frame
# behind (f1830, f2430: the TARGET/NINPO captions not yet drawn) and stays
# one frame off for the rest of the mission. In the three-emulator session
# that one frame changed the fight on a first try at the green gunman: at
# f4078 the ninja was still in the air on nba but had landed on the
# others, and at f4175 nba had killed the gunman (1000 pts) while on
# dingbat-bios/mgba he shot the ninja. On this final route a replay keeps
# nba on track (checkpoints SLIP by 1 frame). dingbat-bios and mgba stayed
# identical throughout.
# The ninja blinks while invulnerable, so some frames show no player.
# EEPROM size: dingbat-bios and mgba write a 512-byte file, nba 8 KB.

